model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Request reliability counts only the retained local model and gateway sources. Explicit purpose records match the exact pool, source and hashed client key; unclassified keys count as real. Proof counts remain visible separately, while token and cost totals retain every request. The same bounded SQL read supplies the overview and rolling one-hour and twenty-four-hour success objectives. Empty real traffic has no success rate. An inactive, stale, lagging or unclassified capture cannot establish the objective. The existing once-per-minute availability monitor reports success below 99 percent and collection unavailability as separate error classes through its existing observability route. Counts and closed reasons leave the service; keys and request content do not."
      constraint "The traffic-purpose schema is an additive named model-history migration applied only through the private reviewed schema operation. It never rewrites request history. Purpose changes use the private operations entrypoint with a dry run listing exact retained request identifiers, current classifications and an evidence hash. Applying requires the digest of that selection; a changed selection refuses. A started local receipt prevents replay after an unknown apply outcome. Restoring a proof key to real uses the same reviewed path. Public app and model routes cannot change purpose."
    }
  }
  basalt.telemetry -[sync]-> basalt.pool "read request reliability contracts for monitor diagnostics"
}
